# The program end of the veth wire keeps its offloads: the kernel sends
# segments of up to 64 KiB, take_frame drops each, and TCP sends each again
# in parts. The flow still passes, slowly; the test of the wire counts the
# frames larger than the MTU and must fail. The test needs a network
# namespace: the check runs it as root (a skip fails it).
ENTRY=T-201
GROUP=hold
EXPECT='frames larger than the MTU on the wire'
RUN='sh scripts/root-netns-tests.sh'
